{"schemaVersion":1,"framework":"react","version":"v0","id":"errors/resource-render","title":"ResourceRenderError","description":"When ResourceRenderError occurs and how to resolve it.","body":[{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["A resource render-state boundary catches an exception while rendering a named state. It wraps the original exception unless it is already a ResourceModuleLoadError or ResourceRenderError."]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:h2","props":{"id":"identify-the-error"},"children":["Identify the error"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":[["The error code is ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["resourceRender"]},". This class extends native ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["Error"]},", independently of ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["ReactLayoutError"]},"."]]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:h2","props":{"id":"resolve-the-error"},"children":["Resolve the error"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Inspect resource, state and cause, then correct the failing render logic. A configured resource Error state can receive this wrapper."]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:h2","props":{"id":"release-scope"},"children":["Release scope"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":[["This page describes ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["@jfdevelops/react-layout@0.25.0"]},". Earlier 0.x releases can differ. The behavior is based on the error definitions and their call sites in ",{"tag":"mdx:a","props":{"href":"https://github.com/jfdevelops/react-layout/blob/%40jfdevelops%2Freact-layout%400.25.0/packages/core/src/errors/resource-state-error.ts"},"children":["the tagged source"]},"."]]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:h2","props":{"id":"next-steps"},"children":["Next steps"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","props":{},"children":[["\n",{"tag":"li","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"mdx:a","props":{"href":"../final-snapshot.md"},"children":["Final snapshot"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"mdx:a","props":{"href":"../standard-schema.md"},"children":["Standard Schema"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","props":{},